---An `PlayerList` provides access to all active PlayerEntities in the game world, as well as several methods to search
---for entities.
---
---Info: All methods, except PlayerList.Self() return an array of PlayerEntities.
---
---See each method for examples on how to use this list.
---@class PlayerList
PlayerList = {}

---Returns the PlayerEntity belonging to the currently logged in player character.
---@return PlayerEntity # A PlayerEntity.
function PlayerList.Self() end

---Returns all active PlayerEntities in the game world in an array.
---@return PlayerEntity[] # An array of PlayerEntities.
function PlayerList.All() end

---Returns the PlayerEntity with the matching UID.
---@param uid integer A valid UID value.
---@return PlayerEntity[] # An array of PlayerEntities.
function PlayerList.ByUID(uid) end

---Returns any PlayerEntity with a display name matching the given `name` value.
---
---String matches are case-insensitive. Matches are exact unless wildcard characters `?` and/or `*` are provided.
---@param name string The string to match against `PlayerEntity.displayName`.
---@return PlayerEntity[] # An array of PlayerEntities.
function PlayerList.ByName(name) end

---Returns any PlayerEntity within `range` tiles of the given `coordGrid` value.
---
---Exact coord matches should use a value of `0` for `range`.
---@param coordGrid CoordGrid The coord at which to centre the distance search.
---@param range integer The maximum tile distance from the given coord which an PlayerEntity must be.
---@return PlayerEntity[] # An array of PlayerEntities.
function PlayerList.ByDistance(coordGrid, range) end

---Returns any PlayerEntity that matches all tests in the `filterSet` table.
---
---Available tests are:
---
---Tests can be combined as shown below:
---
---Info: Tests are inclusive. All must pass in order for the PlayerEntity to be included in the return array.
---@param filterSet PlayerListFilterSettings A table of key-value pairs which describe individual tests to perform.
---@return PlayerEntity[] # An array of PlayerEntities.
function PlayerList.Filter(filterSet) end

---The keys `PlayerList.Filter` takes in its table.
---@class PlayerListFilterSettings
---@field uid integer? A valid entity UID. `{ uid = playerEntity.uid }` See PlayerList.ByUID()
---@field name string? A name to match against `PlayerEntity.displayName`. `{ name = "*GIM*" }` See PlayerList.ByName()
---@field coordGrid CoordGrid? A coord to test entity distance from. If `range` is not provided, the default value of `range` will be `0`. `{ coordGrid = CoordGrid._0_50_50_32_32 }` See PlayerList.ByDistance()
---@field range integer? Ignored if `coordGrid` key is not provided. `{ range = 4 }` See PlayerList.ByDistance()
---@field func (fun(playerEntity: PlayerEntity): boolean)|nil A function which returns a boolean, and which takes a PlayerEntity as its only parameter. This function is called for every entity, and any call that returns `true` will include that PlayerEntity in the return array. `function eastFacingFinder(playerEntity) { return playerEntity.facing == 90 }` `{ func = eastFacingFinder }`
